cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Qur'anic Root & Word Research"
message: >-
  If you use this tool in research, please cite it. Prefer the version DOI
  of the build you actually used: counts and references here are computed
  against one reading of the text and one corpus build, and only that
  snapshot makes a result reproducible.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bahaa
    alias: bahaa-alt
repository-code: "https://github.com/bahaa-alt/Holy-Qur-an"
url: "https://bahaa-alt.github.io/Holy-Qur-an/"
abstract: >-
  A free, open-source, account-less tool for researching Qur'anic Arabic
  roots and word forms. Every derivative and every occurrence, with the
  Uthmani text, two English translations, Tafsir al-Jalalayn, seven
  alternative transmissions, Lane's Lexicon and three classical
  Arabic-Arabic lexicons (Maqayis al-Lugha, al-Mufradat, al-Sihah), a
  syntactic and rhetorical index over 17,014 tagged segments, and QCQL, a
  query language over the corpus. Runs entirely client-side as a static
  export and works offline.
keywords:
  - Quran
  - Arabic
  - corpus linguistics
  - lexicography
  - morphology
  - digital humanities
license: GPL-3.0
# Concept DOI: always resolves to the newest archived version. Cite this
# when referring to the tool in general; cite the version DOI of a specific
# release when a result has to be checkable.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22855797
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-20"
